  "prefLabel": "Ch 101.01 Purpose",
  "priorExpiration": "1999-05-18",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ch 101.01 Purpose. These rules implement the statutory responsibilities of the New Hampshire board of chiropractic examiners created by RSA 316-A:2 which include, but are not limited to:\n\n(a) Establishing the minimum education and experience requirements for licensure as chiropractors;\n\n(b) Establishing the criteria for the examination of applicants for licensure as a chiropractor; and\n\n(c) The development of ethical and other professional standards to be followed by licensees.\n\nSource. #1488, eff 11-20-79; ss by #2052, eff 6-9-82; ss by #2716, eff 5-17-84; ss by #4671, eff 9-7-89; ss by #5624, eff 5-18-93, EXPIRED: 5-18-99\n\nNew. #7516, eff 6-27-01; ss by #14499, eff 3-1-26",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ch100-500.html"
